 ## 1. Goal
-TWL (the browser-only watchlist app) can open a symbol's chart, but once on TradingView you're back to one chart per click. TWLX closes the loop: a chart opened from TWL lets you **step through that watchlist with the keyboard**, in the order and sections you set up in TWL, without leaving the chart.
+Watchlist (the browser-only watchlist app) can open a symbol's chart, but once on TradingView you're back to one chart per click. Watchlist Extension closes the loop: a chart opened from Watchlist lets you **step through that watchlist with the keyboard**, in the order and sections you set up in Watchlist, without leaving the chart.
 
-- No UI on TradingView pages. The extension is a headless bridge plus a toolbar icon.
+- A minimal bookmark control appears only on linked TradingView charts; all other TradingView pages are untouched.
 - No accounts, no backend, no market data, no TradingView login required beyond what TradingView itself needs.
 
 ## 2. Scope
 **In scope:**
-- receiving every TWL list (normal and color lists) from a TWL tab on localhost
-- opening a chart from TWL into **Navigation Mode** (fullscreen)
